    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d847">

                <pb facs="0711" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.516/123</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Representative Rodgers to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-25T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1916, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. In reply to Department’s 54, April 22, 4 p.m. No action as to banks of issue
                    yet; matter still being considered. Moratorium decree dealing with this and
                    matters related thereto delayed but officially informed will be issued soon.</p>
                <p>Present intention with bankers based upon current currency questions anticipatory
                    its new issue. Apparently no progress by Government in matter controlling
                    exchange rate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rodgers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
